From 83a31da1617ed3e39dd67a731ac0e8ffe932e9b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 14:17:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] gugu: do not write the sandbox.json template into the
 user's workspace

readSandboxConfig() used to create `<workspace>/.zcode/acp/sandbox.json`
(enabled:false) on first read, and the backend spawn path reads it for
every workspace, so every project a client opened got a `.zcode/acp/`
directory. A missing file now simply reads as not armed and nothing is
written; a user-created file works exactly as before (including fail-closed
on unreadable / tampered configs).

Why: a client launching the bridge (Gugu) must not leave files in the
user's repository; measured: a fresh workspace got `.zcode/acp/` after one
session/new + prompt.

Upstream: not filed - owner 10-17: kept and maintained here only. Upstream
issue william0wang/zcode-acp#332 asks for the same; see PATCHES.md.

Drop when: upstream stops auto-creating the template (or adds an opt-out we
set) in the tag this is built on.
---
 src/backend/sandbox.ts | 44 ++++++++++++++----------------------------
 tests/sandbox.test.ts  |  6 +++---
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/backend/sandbox.ts b/src/backend/sandbox.ts
index 612d8e3..dc7fc1d 100644
--- a/src/backend/sandbox.ts
+++ b/src/backend/sandbox.ts
@@ -14,8 +14,8 @@
